Kate Middleton had a special guest on  her latest royal outing her  brother-in-law and soon-to-be first-time  dad Prince Harry that's right Harry made  a surprise appearance on Thursday  stepping out with the Duchess of  Cambridge to honor fallen Australian and  New Zealand veterans during the annual  Anzac Day service of commemoration and  Thanksgiving at Westminster Abbey  despite the solemn occasion the pair  were all smiles as they headed inside  Kate in a blue feathered hat matching  coat and green heels Harry in a navy  suit with a red and navy striped tie  both wore red poppy pins a symbol used  since 1921  to commemorate military members who have  died in war the in-law outing comes amid  rumors of tension between Prince William  and Prince Harry the palace have tried  to knock these rumours of attention  between the four Royals on the head and  it does seem to be the case that perhaps  they they don't all get along  as well as we thought that they might do  I think people forget these are still  early days and I think it's a matter of  all of them trying to find their feet as  a foursome for so long we had the royal  trio and you know Harry William and Kate  now of course we've got Megan  but things appear to be a-ok based off  Thursday's appearance and it's no  surprise Harry was grinning ear-to-ear a  royal source tells ET his wife Megan  Merkel is due to give birth to their  first child together quote any day now  they're super excited about the spring  birth of their baby and I'm told that  she's upbeat and that she's happy  Megan's mom Doria Ragland arrived in  London over the weekend in anticipation  of the royal baby's arrival a source  recently told ET megan is enjoying her  pregnancy adding quote it is such a  happy and exciting time for Megan she is  looking forward to becoming a mother  [Music]
 

